instruction:
This C code passed basic linting. Are there deeper security issues?
```c
void copy(char *input) {
    char buf[64];
    strcpy(buf, input);
}
```

output:
Yes — linters typically miss buffer overflow (CWE-119). This is a critical-severity issue.

Use strncpy with bounds checking.

Fix:
```c
void copy(const char *input) {
    char buf[64];
    strncpy(buf, input, sizeof(buf)-1);
    buf[sizeof(buf)-1] = 0;
}
```

