This C code passed basic linting. Are there deeper security issues?
```c
void parse(char *s) {
    char local[128];
    memcpy(local, s, strlen(s));
}
```

output:
Yes — linters typically miss buffer overflow (CWE-119). This is a critical-severity issue.

Check length before memcpy to prevent overflow.

Fix:
```c
void parse(const char *s) {
    size_t len = strlen(s);
    if (len >= 128) return;
    char local[128];
    memcpy(local, s, len);
    local[len] = 0;
}
```

